# Suckless build dependencies — the toolchain and headers needed to compile
# dwm, st, dmenu, dwmblocks and slock from the vendored sources.
#
# CONSUMER: scripts/install-suckless.sh ONLY.
#
# install-pkg.sh does NOT read this list, and that is deliberate.
# install-void.sh runs install-suckless.sh straight after install-pkg.sh
# and without --skip-deps, so the build stage installs its own dependencies
# immediately before it needs them. The useful consequence is that
# --skip-suckless needs no special handling anywhere: skip the build and
# these are never installed, which is exactly right.
#
# FAILURE MODE: hard-fail. install-suckless.sh cannot compile anything
# without these, so there is no degraded mode worth continuing into. This is
# the one list whose failure aborts a stage rather than a feature.
#
# Format: one package name per line. '#' starts a comment (whole-line or
# trailing). Blank lines ignored. Void/xbps names — see the note in
# install-suckless.sh's install_deps() about the pacman/apt fallbacks, which
# cannot be expressed here.

# toolchain
# patch is NOT used by the build. The suckless sources ship pre-patched and
# nothing applies suckless/*/patches/*.diff (CLAUDE.md rule 5 — the diffs are
# a record). It is kept, by the user's decision on 2026-09-28, as the tool for
# hand-merging or re-vendoring a patch on the machine the desktop runs on.
# Know the cost: this tier aborts the build stage on failure, so a missing or
# renamed `patch` would stop a build that does not need it. (Its old comment
# claimed it applied the diffs at build time; it never did.)
# pkgconf resolves freetype/fontconfig for the dwm and st Makefiles.
gcc
make
patch
pkgconf

# X11 — dwm, st and dmenu
libX11-devel
libXft-devel
libXinerama-devel

# X11 — slock additionally needs Xext (DPMS), Xrandr (monitor enumeration)
# and libcrypt (password hashing via crypt(3)).
libXext-devel
libXrandr-devel
libxcrypt-devel

# font rendering — Xft draws through both
freetype-devel
fontconfig-devel

# nsxiv — imlib2 decodes every image format (its loaders bring GIF, WebP,
# HEIC and AVIF; nothing else here is needed for them) and libexif rotates
# photos by their EXIF orientation. Its status bar draws through Xft, already
# listed above. nsxiv was vendored because Fedora did not package it. Void
# does (nsxiv-34_1, the same version), so the vendored copy could be dropped
# for the package. That is an open question in scope I, not changed here.
imlib2-devel
libexif-devel

# bidi + Arabic shaping for dwm's window title and dmenu's lines (the
# bidi-local patches in suckless/{dwm,dmenu}/patches/PATCHES.md)
fribidi-devel

# tic(1), which st's Makefile runs to compile st.info into a terminfo entry
ncurses

# ly, the login screen, built from source by the services stage (scope I,
# decision D1; scripts/install-services-ly.sh). It links PAM and xcb, and its
# zig dependencies ship as a .tar.zst. Listed here so the install stage puts
# them in place before the services stage needs them; the services stage
# checks for them and skips ly, never aborts, when they are missing.
pam-devel
libxcb-devel
zstd
